WEBVTT

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:59.480
Speaking for the International Space Order in the first worldwide radio and telecast in history.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:09.140
At this moment, over two billion people in every part of the world are focusing their attention on this program.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:23.320
Every nation of the earth, in a magnificent effort, is contributing of its people and resources in an attempt to reach the moon and proclaim it international territory.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:29.980
The rocket ship Lunar Eagle No. 1 represents the culminating achievement of the world.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:35.340
world's leading scientists. The men and women who will fly her have been handpicked from

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:41.080
the world's leading specialists. They include Dr. Eric Heinrich, who personally designed

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:46.510
and supervised the construction of this rocket ship. As Dr. Heinrich is the oldest member

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:51.890
of the crew, so Rod Murdoch is the youngest. He holds a doctor's degree in mathematics

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:59.940
at the age of 19. Dr. Salim Hamid from Turkey is an expert on space medicine. She

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.010
Elected to work with him is Dr. Sigrid Beaumont from Sweden, physician and physicist.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:09.780
From France, Etienne Martell, engineer and technician.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.240
Sir William Rochester, noted British geophysicist.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:22.440
Tokyo-born Dr. Hideko Morata will be acting as astrophotographer and pharmacist.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.980
Our shoes represented by Dr. Feodor Orla, geologist and map maker.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:35.920
From Nigeria, the chief navigator, the great astronomer Asmara Makonnen.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.900
From Israel, Polish-born Dr. David Ruskin,

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.440
this aeronautic engineer will serve as the official recorder of this expedition.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:51.780
The Brazilian Dr. Louis Fargus, the ship's first pilot, will also be in charge of communications.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:58.100
The leader of this gigantic undertaking is John Anderson of the United States,

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.980
who has dedicated his life to...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.590
man's conquest of space. His three previous orbital flights have made him

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:10.410
world-famous. Because of his all-around experience, he was the unanimous choice

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:24.720
of the International Space Order to helm this project. In the next few minutes, we

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:29.960
expect to make world-shattering history. The dual-powered Lunar Eagle will take

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.430
off for the liquid fuel method and outside the earth's atmosphere will convert to atomic power

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:43.280
when the moon's orbit is reached by retro power the first landing on the moon will be attempted

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:53.600
if all goes as planned touchdown on lunar soil should be 27 hours from x minus zero during the

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:59.970
entire flight earth control will try to keep in communication with the ship this world

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:06.780
network will bring you bulletins on the flight and the news of the landing. God be with them.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:59.980
We'll be right back.

